###############################################################################################
#                                         NOTE                                                #
#  1. For the 1st column, you should provide sample id. It is recommended giving the id that  #
#     is consistent with SM tag in BAM header if bam/cram sample.                             #
#  2. For the 2nd column, you should provide sex corresponding to the sample id. The single   #
#     character "F" and "M" represents female and male,	respectively.					      #
#  3. For the 3rd column, you should provide sample tag to point out whether the sample is    #
#     case or control. The single character "S" and "C" represents cases and control,         #
#     respectively.                                                                           #
#  4. For the 4th column, it should be the absolute path of bam or cram sample or the read 1  #
#     sequencing fastq sample.                                                                #
#  5. For the 5th column, it should be the absolute path of the read 2 sequencing fastq       #
#	  sample if the 4th column is fastq sample.                                               #
#  6. Mixed input types are allowed.                                                          #
#  7. Non-sample line must be starts with "#".                                                #
#  8. Various file suffix are allowed such as fq, fq.gz, fastq, fastq.gz, bam, cram.          #
###############################################################################################


# sample_id	sex	tag	path1	[path2]
# s1	M	S	s1.bam
# s2	M	S	s2.cram
# s3	F	C	s3.R1.fastq.gz	s3.R2.fastq.gz
# s4	F	C	s4.R1.fq	s4.R2.fq
